# Workspace Switcher Sheet

::summary
The workspace switcher (RULED 08-05), opened from the hub sheet's Switch workspace row: workspace rows with icon chip, name, plan + member-count meta; the ACTIVE workspace row is inert with a trailing accent checkmark; below the separator, Create workspace (name, icon, plan). Shell truth lives in `shell.surf`; this file is the standalone sheet source.
::

::modal[name=workspace-switcher title="Switch workspace" width=320 placement=centered dismissible=true]

:::row[icon=login action=switchToWorkspace href=#]
Personal
Ultra · just you
:::

:::row[icon=task state=current href=#]
cloudsurf — Current
Ultra · 3 members · inert row, trailing accent checkmark
:::

:::row[icon=login action=switchToWorkspace href=#]
ashley-brady
Ultra · 2 members
:::

:::row[icon=doc action=createWorkspace href=#]
Create workspace
Name, icon, plan
:::

::

Top-right ✕ per dismiss canon. Switching re-scopes every surface to the picked workspace; the workspace chip in the top bar re-labels. The rows' `icon=login` / `icon=task` are workspace stand-ins only — the intended treatment is a workspace-initial avatar chip (P, C, AB), which rows cannot express (`blocks.rs:4372` parses `avatar` for toolbar buttons only); the stand-ins stay in markup and this note carries the intent.

At small width (≤ 767px, R-C ruling 08-10) the sheet goes edge-to-edge with 10px side insets and auto width; the wide placement declared on the block is unchanged.
